{
  "id": "ethnic-socialization",
  "term": "ethnic socialization",
  "definition": "Ethnic socialization is the ongoing process by which parents and other caregivers communicate information, values, and viewpoints about race and ethnicity to children. It is a multifaceted part of everyday parenting and family life, including messages that can foster cultural pride, prepare children for bias, encourage caution toward other groups, or emphasize equality and skills for functioning in the broader society.",
